    "ContentType": "html",
    "Content": "<p>Node auto-repair monitors nodes in a cluster and initiates a repair process if a node fails to meet health criteria. This ensures that the nodes in a cluster are always in a healthy, running state.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fazure.microsoft.com%2Fen-us%2Fservices%2Fkubernetes-service%2F&amp;data=02%7C01%7Cv-krwea%40microsoft.com%7C4ea920cae8ac4851a74308d68544d1bc%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C636842927955229218&amp;sdata=tnh9LTP5h%2B5O8B0umDDekbOtmT3D1neYxNgEl0M6wi8%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn more about AKS.</a></p>\r\n",
    "Markdown": "Node auto-repair monitors nodes in a cluster and initiates a repair process if a node fails to meet health criteria. This ensures that the nodes in a cluster are always in a healthy, running state.\n\nLearn more about AKS."
